# Static analysis for the lessons (`make tidy`, and the analyze CI job with a
# pinned clang-tidy 23). The bugprone, clang-analyzer and CERT families stay
# on; the checks below are off because they flag what the course teaches on
# purpose, or flag a safe idiom, and silencing them in the lessons would mean
# NOLINT comments a beginner should not have to read:
#
#   cert-err33-c             every unchecked printf/fprintf/fclose return. The
#                            lessons check the returns that matter (scanf,
#                            fgets, malloc, fopen, and fclose after writing).
#   ...DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling, ...insecureAPI.strcpy
#                            any memcpy, strcpy, strcat or sprintf-family call
#                            (the strcpy check fires only with glibc; macOS
#                            headers hide the calls behind fortify macros).
#                            The lessons that use strcpy/strcat show the
#                            destination is big enough (BUILD.md, unsafe-API
#                            audit).
#   bugprone-signed-bitwise  `1 << 7` style masks in lesson 21.
#   bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion, cert-err34-c
#                            scanf("%d") itself. The lessons check scanf's
#                            return value (lesson 3) and teach strtol for
#                            range checks (lesson 15).
#   bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion
#                            `Entry **e = calloc(...)`: lesson 13 teaches
#                            that void * converts without a cast.
#   clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound
#                            `buf[strcspn(buf, "\n")] = '\0'` after fgets is
#                            reported as a tainted index; it is in bounds.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cert-*,
  -cert-err33-c,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion,
  -cert-err34-c,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
